    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia**_\n\n**Reported:** since #119, opening any prompt with `M-x` hangs Emacs completely on macOS (`C-g` pressed many times eventually shows `[quit]`). Setting `(setq mini-frame-resize 'not-set)` at the end of `sp-mini-frame.el` changed nothing.\n\n**Cause (a guess, not reproduced):** #119 made the frame start at one line (`(height . 1)`), placed it with a computed pixel `top`, set `mini-frame-resize` to `t` and changed the border faces of the open frame on every showing. Since `not-set` did not help, the loop is probably in the frame being resized or restyled while open with a one-line height, which Vertico then needs to be much taller.\n\n**Change:** the pre-#119 pattern with a fixed size:\n- `mini-frame-resize` is `not-set` again; no resizing code, no `mini-frame-resize-max-height`.\n- `(height . N)` with N = `vertico-count` + prompt + divider line, `(left . 0.5)`, `(top . 0.5)` (fractions: centred horizontally and vertically); width `0.6` as before.\n- No `set-face-background` on the open frame; the border colour is set with `mini-frame-internal-border-color` and applies when the frame is made.\n- Colours from the `default` face (#121), 4 pixels padding (#119) unchanged.\n\n**Trade-off:** with fewer than `vertico-count` candidates the frame keeps its size and has empty space at the bottom.\n\n**Not tested:** nothing was run in Emacs, so I cannot confirm this stops the hang. If it still hangs, the next things to try are `(setq sp-mini-frame-divider-char nil)` (removes the overlay) and starting Emacs with `--debug-init` plus `M-x toggle-debug-on-quit` before pressing `M-x`, which shows where it loops.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01MfEFZ7KDkwwcifErLfjf4X)_",
